From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000001 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Webster <webster@webster.is>
Date: Thu, 10 Apr 2026 21:39:04 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat: transparent animated sixel image overlay system

Adds overlay-image command for rendering transparent images as overlays
on the terminal, outside any pane, with live content showing through.

New files:
- cmd-overlay-image.c: 'overlay-image set X Y FILE [-W cols] [-H rows]',
  'overlay-image animate X Y FILE [-W cols] [-H rows]', and
  'overlay-image clear'.  PNG handled natively via libpng; animated GIF
  decoded natively via giflib with per-frame durations.
- image-overlay.c: image_overlay_set/clear/draw/animate.  Animation uses
  libevent timers with per-frame durations from the file metadata.
- image-gif.c: load animated GIF using giflib; composites frames onto an
  RGBA canvas (respecting disposal methods) and encodes via sixel-enc.c.
- sixel-enc.c: RGBA-to-sixel encoder.  Palette deduplication, up to 255
  color registers, RLE output, P2=1 (transparent background).

Modified files:
- tmux.h: struct client image_overlay field; function declarations
- cmd.c: register cmd_overlay_image_entry
- Makefile.am: add new source files; HAVE_GIFLIB conditional block
- configure.ac: detect giflib (optional; enables animate)
- screen-redraw.c: call image_overlay_draw in screen_redraw_pane for
  flicker-free redraws during incremental pane updates (typing/output)
- tty.c: tty_draw_overlay_image with conditional sync (avoids ending
  outer sync block prematurely)
- screen-write.c / input.c: sixel plumbing
---
